# m4/gnulib-cache.m4 into `m4/`, and `m4/gnulib-comp.m4` invokes them all from
# `gl_INIT`.  The list below is exactly those files for which
# `@rules_cc_autoconf//gnulib/m4/` ships an implementation, so it stands in
# for the generated `gl_INIT` body rather than for any choice made here.
# Left out because they are not gnulib configure macros: the libtool set
# (libtool, ltoptions, ltsugar, ltversion, lt~obsolete), the autoconf-archive
# set (ax_*), gnulib-cache/gnulib-comp themselves and wget_manywarnings.
# `memeq`, `streq` and `mbrtoc32-regular` have no port and are written out
# below.
#
# These have to be explicit `deps`: the default autoconf toolchain already
# lists every one of them under `cache_deps`, but that only feeds the content
# cache used to skip duplicate checker actions.  Results reach a consumer's
# `CcAutoconfInfo` only through `deps`.
